when I first visited bonus iris I  immediately fell in love to me there's  no city like this in the entire world my  name is Kristen Borg I'm a travel  enthusiast and a contributor for  National Geographic I first came through  here on my way to Patagonia taking some  time to explore poetess iris is one of  the best decisions I ever made  the moment you step outside you're  immersed in Argentinian culture like at  the delicious Koreas today I'm visiting  el Desna Bell this local Perea is a  traditional restaurant where open fire  drills are used to slow cook local  Argentinian meat into incredibly tender  barbecue  the smell is indescribably good and  permeates the air it was fun to get a  crash course and all the different cuts  of beef served and with all of the  Koreas to choose from across the city  you can find that hidden gem of your own  after lunch I always like to stretch my  legs and there's no better place to do  that than Palermo Park there's a reason  it's so popular with the locals and  nearly a thousand acres it has the most  open space that you can find in the city  centre from unique flower gardens to  boat rides there's so much to do and see  and I know I'll always have the perfect  backdrop for a beautiful photo off the  beaten path is estancia via maria an  old-fashioned hotel on a ranch places  like this are perfect to relax and catch  your breath we got to learn about  Gauchos here the Gauchos are legends in  Argentina they have a rich history  spanning back to the early 1800s helping  Argentina gain independence from Spain  their culture has continued to be passed  down over generations as they work as  ranch hands looking after horses and  preparing meals for the estate seeing  their way of life is an experience in  itself every time I visit Buenos Aires I  wish I would have stayed longer towards  the end of my trips I often find myself  waiting to return  [Music]
 

